Modified files: cli/src/connection.rs, cli/src/mcp.rs, cli/src/output.rs and cli/Cargo.toml, as recorded in kiki-no-replay-r1.patch.
The send_command retry loop was removed. Errors after sending may have begun are marked outcome_unknown and do not trigger daemon respawn/replay. Pre-send connection recovery remains upstream behavior. A Windows isolated lost-response regression counts actual received commands.
Windows MCP output capture drains stdout/stderr while the CLI runs, then consumes buffered bytes after the real CLI exit without waiting for a background process's inherited writer to close. It preserves the real exit code and ordinary output; capture above 64 MiB is an explicit unknown failure. The existing windows-sys pipe API feature is enabled; dependency versions and Cargo.lock are unchanged. An inherited-writer regression verifies capture finishes while the writer remains open. The version display carries both derivative markers.
This is not an unmodified official agent-browser release. No browser engine, MCP tool catalog, or action schema is forked by this patch. This does not promise exactly-once execution across process crashes.
